    elements up to the Nyquist frequency.

    >>> fft2 = torch.fft.fft2(t)
    >>> torch.testing.assert_close(fft2[..., :6], rfft2, check_stride=False)

    The discrete Fourier transform is separable, so :func:`~torch.fft.rfft2`
